    <bpmn:process id="W_W4033" name="W4033. Election-Period Compliance Protocol (Omnibus Election Code, RA 9006, COMELEC)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Election period declared (national/local/Barangay/SK/BARMM); COMELEC resolution
Frequency: Per election cycle
Volume: All 5 entities, 200 stores, all regions
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Participants: Legal (links to VS-100), Compliance (links to VS-119), Govt Affairs (links to VS-104), Marketing (links to VS-14), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Corporate Communications (links to VS-14.3), regional teams
Source: workflow W4033 — Election-Period Compliance Protocol (Omnibus Election Code, RA 9006, COMELEC)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4033_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4033_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4033_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4033_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4033_Lane2" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4033_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4033_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4033_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4033_Start4" name="Election period declared (national/local/Barangay/SK/BARMM); COMELEC resolution">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4033_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4033_Task5" name="VP Legal activate the election-period compliance protocol on COMELEC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VP Legal activate the election-period compliance protocol on COMELEC election-period declaration: communicate restrictions across all entities/stores/regions (no corporate contributions, no partisan activity, election-period advertising rules, no use of company resources for partisanship), and align Marketing/Comms/Store-Ops to the restrictions
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Compliance / Govt Affairs
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4033_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4033_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4033_Task6" name="Legal/Marketing implement election-period advertising/marketing restrictions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Legal/Marketing implement election-period advertising/marketing restrictions (COMELEC rules on election propaganda, airtime/print limits, blackout periods, and the risk that BuildRight promotions/ads could be construed as indirect candidate/party support), with pre-publication review of sensitive campaigns
Responsible (R): Legal / Marketing / Comms
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4033_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4033_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4033_Task7" name="Legal/Compliance monitor compliance during the cycle, manage incidents (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Legal/Compliance monitor compliance during the cycle, manage incidents (links to VS-119), and document the cycle for disclosure (links to W4032) and lessons (links to W4040)
Responsible (R): Legal / Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4033_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4033_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4033_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4033_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-161 (ensure election-period &amp; political-contribution compliance.) | - operational: protocol and pre-publication review; operational: enterprise-wide communication
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4033_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4033_Annotation9" targetRef="W4033_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4033_Flow11" sourceRef="W4033_Start4" targetRef="W4033_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4033_Flow12" sourceRef="W4033_Task5" targetRef="W4033_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4033_Flow13" sourceRef="W4033_Task6" targetRef="W4033_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4033_Flow14" sourceRef="W4033_Task7" targetRef="W4033_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
